    key = "x",
    value = eval("obj." + key);

(0, eval)("var a = 0");

var foo = eval;
foo("var a = 0");

// This `this` is the global object.
this.eval("var a = 0");
```

Example of additional incorrect code for this rule when `browser` environment is set to `true`:


```json
